{"batchcomplete":"","query":{"pages":{"6267555":{"pageid":6267555,"ns":6,"title":"File:2009 DC Proof.png","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":786437,"width":1078,"height":1081,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/2009_DC_Proof.png/960px-2009_DC_Proof.png","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":642,"responsiveUrls":{"2":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/2009_DC_Proof.png"},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/cf/2009_DC_Proof.png","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2009_DC_Proof.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=6267555","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2009-03-18 21:12:44","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"2009 DC Proof","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"PD US money|United States coins with transparent background|DC and US Territories quarter (District of Columbia)","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"ImageDescription":{"value":"<p>Washington, D.C. state quarter.\n</p>\n<table class=\"licensetpl\" style=\"display:none\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span class=\"licensetpl_short\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_long\">Public domain</span><span class=\"licensetpl_link_req\">false</span><span class=\"licensetpl_attr_req\">false</span>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<table style=\"width: 100%; clear: both; margin: 0.5em auto; background-color: var(--background-color-progressive-subtle, #f7f8ff); color: var(--color-base, #202122); border: var(--border-subtle, 2px solid #8888aa); border-spacing: 8px; padding: 0px;\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"layouttemplate\" lang=\"en\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><figure class=\"mw-halign-left noresize\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><span title=\"Public domain\"><img alt=\"Public domain\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/PD-icon.svg/120px-PD-icon.svg.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/PD-icon.svg/250px-PD-icon.svg.png 2x\" data-file-width=\"196\" data-file-height=\"196\"></span><figcaption>Public domain</figcaption></figure>\n</td>\n<td><i>This image depicts a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:money\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:money\">unit of currency</a> issued by the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:United States\">United States</a> of America. If this is an image of paper currency or a coin not listed <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.usmint.gov/policies/terms-of-use#rights\">here</a>, it is solely a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/work_of_the_United_States_Government\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:work of the United States Government\">work of the United States Government</a>, is ineligible for US <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/copyright\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:copyright\">copyright</a>, and is therefore in the <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/public_domain\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:public domain\">public domain</a></b> in the United States.</i><br><i><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:fraud\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:fraud\">Fraudulent</a> use of this image is punishable under applicable <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/counterfeit\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:counterfeit\">counterfeiting</a> laws.</i><br>\n<p><i>As listed by the the U.S. Currency Education Program at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.uscurrency.gov/media/currency-image-use\">money illustrations</a>, the Counterfeit Detection Act of 1992, Public Law 102-550, in Section 411 of Title 31 of the Code of Federal Regulations (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/31/411.1\">31 CFR 411</a>), permits color illustrations of U.S. currency provided:<br>1. The illustration is of a size less than three-fourths or more than one and one-half, in linear dimension, of each part of the item illustrated;<br>2. The illustration is one-sided; and<br>3. All negatives, plates, positives, digitized storage medium, graphic files, magnetic medium, optical storage devices, and any other thing used in the making of the illustration that contain an image of the illustration or any part thereof are destroyed and/or deleted or erased after their final use.</i><br>\n<i>Certain coins contain copyrights licensed to the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._Mint\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:U.S. Mint\">U.S. Mint</a> and owned by third parties </i>or<i> assigned to and owned by the U.S. Mint <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.usmint.gov/policies/terms-of-use#rights\">[1]</a>. For the United States Mint circulating coin design use policy, see <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.usmint.gov/news/consumer-alerts/business-guidelines/circulating-coin-design-use-policy\">[2]</a>; for the policy on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/50_State_Quarters\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:50 State Quarters\">50 State Quarters</a>, see <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"https://www.usmint.gov/news/consumer-alerts/business-guidelines/50-state-quarters-design-use-policy\">[3]</a>.</i>\n</p><p><i>Also: <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Commons:ART#Photograph_of_an_old_coin_found_on_the_Internet\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Commons:ART\">COM:ART #Photograph of an old coin found on the Internet</a></i>\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2009-03-18","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Credit":{"value":"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.usmint.gov/pressroom/index.cfm?flash=yes&amp;action=photo\">http://www.usmint.gov/pressroom/index.cfm?flash=yes&amp;action=photo</a> United States Mint","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"United States Mint","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}}}]}}}}